# perf run evidence: the raw sample bundles are host- and build-specific and
# run to multiple gigabytes, so they stay local and are regenerated by
# scripts/perf-mc-host.sh. Only the bulk subdirectories are ignored. The frozen
# contract requires docs/perf/ to retain the run report, manifest, environment,
# and integrity hashes, so those top-level files stay tracked: a clean checkout
# can then audit which artifact produced a decision, and verify a local bundle
# against committed hashes, even though it cannot hold the samples themselves.
docs/perf/runs/*/*/
# ...but analysis code is not bulk evidence. A committed report that rests on a
# post-hoc correction is only auditable if the script implementing it ships too,
# so the code is retained while its multi-megabyte outputs are not.
!docs/perf/runs/*/analysis/
docs/perf/runs/*/analysis/*
!docs/perf/runs/*/analysis/*.py

# Standalone dashboard DB adapter build artifacts
packages/dashboard/db-adapter/target/
